{#
  The image node-exporter's `ghcr-mirror-pull` sidecar GETs through each node's ghcr.io mirror
  endpoint (#5542): nut's own, at the content tag this render pulls. nut is the image the
  mirror exists for, because it must cold-start during a WAN outage. Only nut's render sees
  that tag (`k8s_built_image_tags` holds a role's own builds alone), so the tag ships from
  here and the sidecar mounts this ConfigMap from node-exporter's role.

  No pod of this role names it, so a tag move adds nothing to nut's `checksum/restart`; the
  tag move rolls nut through its image ref anyway. The sidecar re-reads the mount on every
  write, so node-exporter does not roll either. The repository and the tag are separate keys,
  never one `<repo>:<tag>` string, so the renderer's built-image ref scan does not read this
  file as a ref. The repository is the one promote pushes to, under
  `scripts/renderer/renderer_lib/images.py:GHCR`.
#}
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: nut-ghcr-mirror-probe
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
data:
  repository: danielh2018/nut
  tag: "{{ nut_k8s_image.rsplit(':', 1)[1] }}"
